  1. [root prerequisite] Ensure dedicated account/group akwaaba-indexer exists with home /srv/solanaghana/projects/akwaaba-indexer and no login shell; reject an unrelated existing account
  2. Ensure platform-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '755' '/srv/solanaghana/projects'
  3. Ensure platform-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '755' '/srv/solanaghana/deployments'
  4. Ensure platform-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '755' '/srv/solanaghana/configs'
  5. Ensure platform-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '755' '/srv/solanaghana/logs'
  6. Ensure platform-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '755' '/srv/solanaghana/systemd'
  7. Ensure project-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'akwaaba-indexer' '-g' 'akwaaba-indexer' '-m' '750' '/srv/solanaghana/projects/akwaaba-indexer'
  8. Ensure project-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'akwaaba-indexer' '-g' 'akwaaba-indexer' '-m' '750' '/srv/solanaghana/deployments/akwaaba-indexer'
  9. Ensure project-owned directory
     $ [root] 'install' '-d' '-o' 'akwaaba-indexer' '-g' 'akwaaba-indexer' '-m' '750' '/srv/solanaghana/logs/akwaaba-indexer'
 10. First deployment: clone backend
     $ [user=akwaaba-indexer] 'git' 'clone' '--depth' '1' '--branch' 'production' '--' 'https://github.com/user/akwaaba-indexer' '/srv/solanaghana/projects/akwaaba-indexer/backend'
 11. Build backend (include dependency installation in this command)
     $ [user=akwaaba-indexer] cd '/srv/solanaghana/projects/akwaaba-indexer/backend' && '/bin/sh' '-c' 'cargo build --release'
 12. [root prerequisite] Render fresh units and Caddy fragment into platform-owned staging; validate units before installation. Do not install stale files.
 13. Install backend unit
     $ [root] 'install' '-o' 'root' '-g' 'root' '-m' '644' '/srv/solanaghana/systemd/akwaaba-indexer-backend.service' '/etc/systemd/system/akwaaba-indexer-backend.service'
 14. Reload systemd
     $ [root] 'systemctl' 'daemon-reload'
 15. Enable backend
     $ [root] 'systemctl' 'enable' 'akwaaba-indexer-backend.service'
 16. Start or restart backend with the updated code
     $ [root] 'systemctl' 'restart' 'akwaaba-indexer-backend.service'
 17. No domain is configured, so Caddy is left untouched
 18. Execution is not implemented. Stop on any failure. In-place updates are not atomic and have no rollback or application health check.
